# Build context of the Airflow image (docker-compose.yml: context ".", infrastructure/airflow/Dockerfile).
# The Dockerfile copies only these files; everything else stays out of the context, including
# container-owned data the build cannot read (dev/volumes/postgres/data), downloaded data and logs.
# The backend and frontend images build from their own folders and are not affected.
# When the Dockerfile COPYs a new file, list it here too.
*
!pipelines/requirements.txt
!pipelines/dbt/requirements.txt
